      "text": "To determine the number of distinct numbers in the list \n\\[\n\\left\\lfloor \\frac{1^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor, \\ \\left\\lfloor \\frac{2^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor, \\ \\left\\lfloor \\frac{3^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor, \\ \\dots, \\ \\left\\lfloor \\frac{1000^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor,\n\\]\nwe need to analyze the expression \\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor\\).\n\nFirst, consider the smallest term:\n\\[\n\\left\\lfloor \\frac{1^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{1}{1000} \\right\\rfloor = 0.\n\\]\nAs \\(n\\) increases, we have:\n\\[\n\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor.\n\\]\n\nNext, we determine the upper bound for \\(n\\):\n\\[\n\\left\\lfloor \\frac{m^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor \\leq m \\quad \\text{for} \\quad m \\leq 1000.\n\\]\nThis can be shown by using the inequality:\n\\[\n\\frac{m^2}{1000} \\leq m + 999,\n\\]\nmeaning:\n\\[\nm^2 \\leq 1000m + 999000 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad m^2 - 1000m - 999000 \\leq 0.\n\\]\nSolving the quadratic inequality \\(m^2 - 1000m - 999000 \\leq 0\\) using quadratic formula:\n\\[\nm = \\frac{1000 \\pm \\sqrt{1000^2 + 4 \\cdot 999000}}{2}.\n\\]\nCalculate:\n\\[\n1000^2 + 4 \\cdot 999000 = 1000000 + 3996000 = 4996000.\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sqrt{4996000} \\approx 2235.14.\n\\]\nThus:\n\\[\nm = \\frac{1000 \\pm 2235.14}{2}.\n\\]\nTaking the positive root:\n\\[\nm \\approx 1117.57,\n\\]\nrounding down:\n\\[\nm \\leq 1000.\n\\]\nSo the highest possible value of \\(m\\) is \\(1000\\).\n\nThe possible values for \\(n\\) range from \\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{1}{1000} \\right\\rfloor\\) to \\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{1000^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor\\):\n\\[\nn = 0 \\quad to \\quad 1000.\n\\]\n\nCalculating \\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor\\) for each \\(n\\):\n\\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{0^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor = 0\\),\n\\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{1^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor = 0\\),\n\\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{2^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor = 0\\),\nand so on, up to:\n\\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{1000^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor = 1000\\).\n\nThe list, after removing duplicates, consists of all integers \\(k\\) from:\n\\(\\left\\lfloor 0 \\right\\rfloor\\) to \\(\\left\\lfloor 1000^2 / 1000 \\right\\rfloor = 1000\\).\n\nThe set \\(\\left\\{0, 1, 2, 3, \\ldots, 1000 \\right\\}\\) contains 1001 distinct numbers.\n\nThus, the number of distinct numbers in the list is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1001}\n\\]",
